{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790502810,"nonce":"O+IRpTIFDc0zEvaIO638G1bK54k=","title":"Drop insertion: a loop-carried pair of phis never agrees on a release, so its objects leak","message":"release_owned_phis decides each owning phi's release from its incomings in rounds, and a phi takes one only when every incoming's release is already known. A loop-carried value is a header phi and a merge phi naming each other (scimark LU_factor's running maximum `t`: header phi [initial, merge phi], merge phi [header phi, candidate]), so neither is ever known and both lose ownership. Since the fix for 3a67874 the phis handing their objects to such a pair lose ownership too, so every boxed candidate in LU's pivot search (and the running maximum) is left unreleased: one box per inner iteration leaks.\n\nResolving the release over the connected web of candidate phis (all sites reaching it agree, or none owns) would let the pair own and release what it replaces. Reproducer: crates/compiler/tests/owned_phi_release.rs builds the shape; after drop_insert no Free of the join phi or of the running value is placed. ZYNTAX_TRACE_DROP=1 on scimark_lu shows the candidates dropped.","files":null}]}